PCA:
Principle component analysis:
1 No target so it is comes under unsupervised algorithm
2 This can also be used in the preprocessing
3 PCA converts the any no of column in to a specific column
4.PCA can also be called as "Dimensionality Reduction Technique"
5.It converts highly correlated data in to non corelated data
6.It can also uded for visualization ,when i want to project high dimension in to  lower dimension

Note:
When we have column which is similar an you can't choose any column because all the column
a.looks same and fine, then you should choose pca.
b.pca wont be selecting the column instead it creates a new column
c.no of new colum tat we needed will be decided on n_components parameter

Flow of working:
1.So PCA also needs data to be standardized
2.It calculates the co-variance matrix(summary about the relationship about the data or variables or
2.1 Positive co-variance(1.0)
2.2 Negative co-variance(-1.0)
2.3 unrelated(0)
3.We will be calculating the distance (Eigen values,Eigenvector)

